   - **Risk for children:** If one parent has Marshan syndrome, there is a 50% chance that their parents will inherit the mutation and a 50% chance that they will not.
   - **Mosaic mutations:** In some cases, the mutation may arise spontaneously (mosaic mutation) in the child's body, which means that the child will not be able to pass the mutation to their parents or their children.

