"What is the definition of whole body oxygen delivery, and how is it calculated?","<bos><start_of_turn>user
What is the definition of whole body oxygen delivery, and how is it calculated?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The definition of whole body oxygen delivery is the rate at which oxygen is available to the body's tissues. It is a measure of the body's ability to supply oxygen to the body's cells, which are essential for cellular respiration and energy production.

Oxygen delivery is influenced by several factors, including oxygen intake, oxygen content in the blood, and the rate at which blood is transported to the tissues.

Oxygen demand is the rate at which the body's tissues require oxygen to maintain their function. Oxygen demand is influenced by factors such as metabolic activity, temperature, and stress.

