Phos-Flur Rinse contains sodium fluoride at a concentration of 0.044% (w/v). How many milligrams of sodium fluoride are present in a 10 mL dose?,"<bos><start_of_turn>user
Phos-Flur Rinse contains sodium fluoride at a concentration of 0.044% (w/v). How many milligrams of sodium fluoride are present in a 10 mL dose?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","To find the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Fol rinse, follow these steps:

1. **Understand the concentration:** 0.044% (w/v) means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride are dissolved in 100 mL of solution.

2. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:**
   \[
   \text{Mass of NaF} = \left( \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} \right) \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
   \]

3. **Convert grams to milligrams:**
   \[
   \text{Mass of NaF} = 0.0044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
   \]

   Therefore, there are \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose.",relevance,"# Task Description
