","Chronic stress can significantly affect the functionality of natural killer cells (NK cells) in the immune system. NK cells are a type of immune cell that are essential for the elimination of viruses, bacteria, and cancer cells. They are unique because they can divide into two types of NK cells: excitatory and inhibitory NK cells. NK cells are activated by the presence of viral or cancer cells, which are exposed by the release of specific molecules. NK cells are inhibited by the presence of normal cells, which express specific molecules that prevent the NK cells from attacking them. NK cells are essential for maintaining the balance between the immune and non-immune systems.  

