   - MCTs are a type of fatty acid that is digested and metabolized differently than long-chain triglycerides (TCGs), which are the most common type of fat in our diet. MCTs are shorter in length and are more easily digested and absorbed by the small lining of the intestines.
   - MCTs are more likely to be used for energy and are less likely to be stored as fat in the body compared to TCGs.
   - Studies on MCTs and weight loss are mixed, with some showing positive effects and others not.

