<GROUND_TRUTH>
The results are inconclusive. A positive ELISA for HIV-1 antibodies must be confirmed by Western blot, which requires the presence of at least two specific bands (e.g., gp120/160 and p24) for a definitive diagnosis. A single band at gp160 is insufficient to confirm HIV-1 infection, especially in the absence of clinical symptoms and with a normal CD4 T-cell count. Further testing, such as repeat Western blot or nucleic acid testing (NAT), is needed to resolve the discrepancy. 

