The entropy change (\( \Delta S \)) for a reaction is calculated using the following formula:

\[
\Delta S = \Sigma S_f^\circ(\text{products}) - \Sigma S_f^\circ(\text{reactants})
\]

Substituting the given molar entropies:

\[
\Delta S = [2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2] - [2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1]
\]

\[
\Delta S = [133 + 496.4] - [182.4 + 615.3]
\]

\[
\Delta S = 629.4 - 797.7
\]

\[
\Delta S = -168.3 \text{ J/mol K}
\]

Thus, the entropy change for the given reaction is \(\boxed{-168.3 \text{ J/mol K}}\).
