<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The coefficient of friction (\( \mu \)) is dimensionless, meaning it has no units. This is because it is defined as the ratio of the frictional force (\( f \)) to the normal force (\( N \)):  
\[
\mu = \frac{f}{N}
\]  
Since \( f \) has units of force (\( [MLT^{-2}] \)) and \( N \) has units of force (\( [MLT^{-2}] \)), the coefficient of friction is dimensionless:  
\[
\mu = \frac{[MLT^{-2}]}{[MLT^{-2}]} = [M^0L^0T^0]
\]  
Thus, the correct answer is \(\boxed{c}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

