2. Enhanced densening: The presence of Si doping can enhance the densening of the TiO2 nanotubes during sintering. This is due to the formation of Si-rich phases, which can act as a liquid phase at high temperatures, promoting the diffusion of TiO2 grains and promoting neck neck formation between them.

3. Enhanced grain growth: The presence of Si doping can also lead to enhanced grain growth of the TiO2 phase, particularly at higher temperatures. This is due to the formation of Si-rich phases, which can act as a liquid phase at high temperatures, promoting the diffusion of TiO2 grains and promoting neck neck formation between them.

4. Enhanced mechanical properties: The presence of Si doping can lead to enhanced mechanical properties of the TiO2 nanotubes, such as increased strength and hardness. This is due to the formation of Si-rich phases, which can act as a barrier to crack propagation and improve the overall strength of the material.

