  \]

(c) **1-Butanol (C₄H₁₀O)**  
- The molecular ion (m/z 74) can lose water (H₂O, mass 18), yielding a peak at m/z 56.  
- Fragmentation:  
  \[
  \text{C}_4\text{H}_{10}\text{O}^+ \rightarrow \text{C}_4\text{H}_8^+ \, (\text{m/z 56}) + \text{H}_2\text{O}
  \]

(d) **Ethylbenzene (C₈H₁₀)**  
- The molecular ion (m/z 106) undergoes alpha-cleavage to lose an ethyl radical (·C₂H₅, mass 29), yielding a peak at m/z 77 (tropylium ion).  
