   \[
   \text{Area} = \text{length} \times \text{width} = 50 \text{ m} \times 16.5 \text{ m} = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]

3. **Let the width of each paving stone be \( x \) cm.**  
   \[
   \text{Width of each paving stone} = x \text{ m}
   \]

4. **Calculate the area of one paving stone:**  
   \[
   \text{Area of one paving stone} = 2.5 \text{ m} \times x \text{ m} = 2.5x \text{ m}^2
   \]

5. **Total area of all paving stones:**  
   \[
   \text{Total area} = 165 \text{ paving stones} \times 2.5x \text{ m}^2 = 412.5x \text{ m}^2
   \]

6. **Set the total area of the paving stones equal to the area of the courtyard:**  
   \[
   412.5x = 825
   \]

7. **Solve for \( x \):**  
   \[
   x = \frac{825}{412.5} = 2
   \]

   The width of each paving stone is \(\boxed{2 \text{ m}}\).
