","The voltage gain of the amplifier with negative feedback is given by:  
\[ A_{vf} = \frac{A_v}{1 - m_v} \]  
Substituting the given values:  
\[ A_{vf} = \frac{100}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{100}{0.9} \approx 111.11 \, \text{dB} \]  

The gain \( A_v \) decreases by 6 dB due to ageing, so the new \( A_v' = 100 - 6 = 94 \).  

The new closed-loop gain \( A_{vf}' \) is:  
\[ A_{vf}' = \frac{94}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{94}{0.9} \approx 104.44 \, \text{dB} \]  

The percentage change in the closed-loop gain is:  
\[ \text{Percentage change} = \left( \frac{A_{vf}' - A_{vf}}{A_{vf}} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{104.44 - 111.11}{111.11} \right) \times 100 \]  
\[ \text{Percentage change} = \left( \frac{-6.67}{111.11} \right) \times 100 \approx -6.01\% \]  

