(b) The time it takes for the proton to reach a speed of \(35,000 \, \text{m/s}\) is calculated using the kinematic equation:  
\[
v = v_0 + at
\]  
Since the proton starts from rest, \(v_0 = 0\).  
\[
35,000 \, \text{m/s} = 0 + (4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2) t
\]  
Solving for \(t\):  
\[
t = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2} = 7.25 \times 10^{-9} \, \text{s}
