- \( R = 8.314 \) J/mol·K (universal gas constant)
- \( T = 300 \) K (temperature, assuming 1 atm = 1 atm and 1 atm = 1 atm, so \( T = \frac{2 \times 10^5}{101.325} = 1980 \text{ K} \), but the reference document suggests \( T = 300 \text{ K} \), which is more reasonable for an isothermal process).
