\]
where \( \hbar \) is the reduced Planck constant, \( m \) is the mass of the molecule, \( k_B \) is the Boltzmann constant, and \( T \) is the temperature.

The integral over the momentum coordinates \( d^3 p \) yields:
\[
\int d^3 p \exp\left( -\frac{\hbar^2 \vec{p}^2}{2m k_B T} \right) = \frac{4\pi \pi^3}{2\pi \hbar^2} \left( \frac{k_B T}{\hbar} \right)^{3/2} = \frac{4\pi}{3} \left( \frac{k_B T}{\hbar} \right)^{3/2}
